ore_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.009111094486154537,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":1.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.06812468713902975,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.1468325565077933,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.15019,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Axsome Therapeutics, Inc., a biopharmaceutical company, develops and delivers novel therapies for the management of central nervous system (CNS) disorders in the United States. The company's commercial product portfolio includes Auvelity (dextromethorphan-bupropion), a N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor antagonist, sigma-1 receptor agonist, aminoketone, and CYP2D6 inhibitor indicated for the treatment of major depressive disorder in adults; Sunosi (solriamfetol), a dopamine and norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor, trace amine-associated receptor 1 agonist, and 5-HT1A agonist indicated for the treatment of excessive daytime sleepiness in patients with narcolepsy or obstructive sleep apnea; and Symbravo (MoSEIC meloxicam rizatriptan), or AXS-07, a rapidly absorbed, multi-mechanistic, selective COX-2 inhibitor, and 5-HT1B/1D agonist indicated for the acute treatment of migraine with or without aura. It also develops AXS-05 (dextromethorphan-bupropion), an investigational N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor antagonist, which has completed Phase III clinical trial to treat Alzheimer's disease agitation, as well as that has completed phase II clinical trial for the treatment of smoking cessation; AXS-12 (reboxetine), a highly selective and potent norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor and cortical dopamine modulator, which has completed Phase II trial to treat narcolepsy; AXS-14 (esreboxetine), a selective and potent norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor that has completed Phase III trial for the treatment of fibromyalgia and other conditions; and Solriamfetol, a dopamine and norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor, which is in Phase III trial for treating attention deficit hyperactivity, major depressive, binge eating, and excessive sleepiness associated with shift work disorder. It has a research collaboration agreement with Duke University for evaluating AXS-05 in a Phase 2 clinical trial in smoking cessation treatment. The company was incorporated in 2012 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Herriot  Tabuteau M.D. | Founder, Chairman, CEO & President | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $459K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $67K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Axsome Therapeutics, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.5B market cap on $638M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +54% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -74% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $94M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Net dilution runs at 0.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 26% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $43.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-43285092.39},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 417% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-mont